---
import LegalPage from "../components/LegalPage.astro";

const sections = [
  ["overview", "Overview"],
  ["local-first", "Local-first storage"],
  ["third-party", "Third-party providers"],
  ["permissions", "Device permissions"],
  ["attribution", "Open-source attribution"],
] as const;
---

<LegalPage
  title="Privacy Policy | Sovereign"
  description="How Sovereign handles local data, connected services, and privacy choices."
  heading="Sovereign Privacy Policy"
  lede="Sovereign is an open-source, self-hosted control plane for coding agents. Your threads, source code, and credentials stay on your own devices and environments unless you connect an external provider."
  effectiveDate="2026-11-25"
  lastUpdated="2026-11-25"
  sections={sections}
>
  <section id="overview">
    <p class="section-number">01</p>
    <h2>Overview</h2>
    <p>
      Sovereign is an independent, MIT-licensed open-source software project. When you run
      Sovereign locally or on your own servers, your application state, settings, and thread
      history remain under your control.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you operate a self-hosted Sovereign deployment, relay, or marketing site, you are
      responsible for publishing and enforcing the privacy practices that govern your deployment.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="local-first">
    <p class="section-number">02</p>
    <h2>Local-First Storage</h2>
    <p>
      Sovereign stores connection settings, preferences, drafts, and cached thread and repository
      metadata on your device and in your configured environment database. Credentials and session
      tokens use platform-provided protected storage where supported.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="third-party">
    <p class="section-number">03</p>
    <h2>Third-Party Providers</h2>
    <p>
      When you connect coding agents, AI providers, source-control hosts, or optional relay
      services, those third parties process prompts, source files, and metadata under their own
      terms and privacy policies.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="permissions">
    <p class="section-number">04</p>
    <h2>Device Permissions</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Camera.</strong> Used only when you scan a pairing QR code. Camera frames are
        processed on your device.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Photos and files.</strong> Accessed only when you choose items to preview or attach
        to a prompt.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Microphone.</strong> Used only when you initiate voice input.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Local network.</strong> Used to discover or connect to Sovereign environments over
        your network.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section id="attribution">
    <p class="section-number">05</p>
    <h2>Open-Source Attribution</h2>
    <p>
      Sovereign is an independent open-source project built upon T3 Code under the MIT License
      (Copyright (c) 2026 T3 Tools Inc.) and is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or maintained by
      T3 Tools, Inc.
    </p>
  </section>
</LegalPage>
